    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47289" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Syrĭarcha</span></b> , ae,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Συριάρχης,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the chief
			priest</i> in Syria, Cod. Th. 15, 9, 2; called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Syrĭarchus</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Just.
				Nov. 89, 15</span></i>.— <i>His office</i>
			is called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Syrĭarchĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Συριαρχία,</span> Cod. Th. 12, 1, 103.</div>
